[0.00763, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ claude\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m> PROMPT:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.00976, "o", "  Read CLAUDE.md. Create src/data/universities.json with 84 real universities following the data model exactly.\r\n  \r\n  Requirements:\r\n  - Global spread: ~22 North America (US + Canada), ~24 Europe (UK, Germany, Netherlands, France, Switzerland, Italy, Spain, Nordics, Ireland), ~20 Asia (Japan, South Korea, Singapore, Hong Kong, China, India, Malaysia), ~8 Oceania (Australia, NZ), ~10 Middle East + rest (UAE, Qatar, Turkey, Israel, Saudi Arabia)\r\n  - Mix of selectivity: elite (minGPA 3.7+), strong (3.3–3.7), solid (2.8–3.3), accessible (2.2–2.8) — roughly a quarter each\r\n  - Realistic international tuition (e.g., German publics near zero, UK £, US privates high), realistic living costs per city, real application fees, approximate world ranking bands, real websites\r\n  - Every university gets 3–6 field tags from the canonical list only\r\n  - Values should be sensible estimates a tutorial viewer would find credible; exact precision is not required\r\n  \r\n  Then create src/lib/loadUniversities.js that imports the JSON and exports it with derived field `totalAnnualUSD = tuitionIntlUSD + livingCostUSD`.\r\n  Write a small validation script scripts/validate-data.mjs (node) that checks every record against the schema (required keys, tag validity, numeric ranges) and run it until the dataset passes. Add \"validate\" to package.json scripts.\r\n"]
[0.009954, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- Claude Code session start ---\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[229.529834, "o", "Done. Summary:\r\n\r\n- **`src/data/universities.json`** — 84 real universities: 22 North America, 24 Europe, 20 Asia, 8 Oceania, 10 Middle East, matching the CLAUDE.md data model exactly (id, name, country, city, region, minGPA, acceptanceRate, fields, tuitionIntlUSD, livingCostUSD, applicationFeeUSD, ranking, website). Selectivity is split roughly into quarters (21 elite / 23 strong / 20 solid / 20 accessible), each with 3–6 canonical field tags and realistic tuition/living/fee/ranking estimates (e.g. German/Swiss publics near-zero tuition, US private elites ~$58–65k, UK/Asia/Oceania priced per real patterns).\r\n- **`src/lib/loadUniversities.js`** — imports the JSON and adds the derived `totalAnnualUSD` field.\r\n- **`scripts/validate-data.mjs`** — checks required keys, region/tag validity, numeric ranges, id uniqueness, and website format; added as `npm run validate`.\r\n\r\n`npm run validate` passes (84/84 OK) and `npm run build` still succeeds.\r\n"]
[229.803461, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- session complete (exit 0) ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
